      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported a positive prior year development (release) of GBP 11.5 million, representing 9.53% of its opening net claims outstanding of GBP 120.707 million. This release was primarily due to favorable claims development on long tail lines and recalibration of IBNR, reflecting emerging experience as the Syndicate's live business matures. In 2018, the syndicate was impacted by catastrophe activity, including Hurricane Michael (GBP 3.5m), Typhoon Jebi (GBP 2.8m), Camp fire (GBP 2.8m), Hurricane Florence (GBP 1.8m), and Typhoon Trami (GBP 1.4m). The net loss ratio decreased to 60% in 2018 from 101% in 2017, largely due to the impact of Hurricanes Harvey, Irma and Maria in 2017 (net impact GBP 12.2m).",
